//
// Normative rule senvcfg_sse_Zicfiss (src/priv/supervisor.adoc):
//   The Zicfiss extension adds the SSE field in senvcfg. When the SSE field is set to 1, the
//     Zicfiss extension is activated in VU/U-mode. When the SSE field is 0, the Zicfiss extension
//     remains inactive in VU/U-mode, and the following rules apply:
//
// Context:
//   The rules: 32-bit Zicfiss instructions revert to Zimop, 16-bit ones to Zcmop, and "When
//     menvcfg.SSE is one, SSAMOSWAP.W/D raises an illegal-instruction exception in U-mode and a
//     virtual-instruction exception in VU-mode." satp and vsatp are Bare, so an active shadow-stack
//     access raises a store/AMO access fault (satp_mode_bare), which shows activation without
//     paging.
//
// Clarifications:
//   https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/2424: VU-mode ssamoswap with senvcfg.SSE=0
//     raises virtual-instruction.
//
