//   1. menvcfg.SSE=1, henvcfg.SSE=1, senvcfg.SSE=0: U-mode and VU-mode ssrdp write 0;
//     sspush/sspopchk (and with Zcmop c.sspush/c.sspopchk) do nothing.
//   2. ssamoswap: illegal-instruction in U-mode, virtual-instruction in VU-mode (xtval 0 or the
//     instruction bits).
//   3. S-mode is unaffected: ssrdp returns ssp.
//   4. senvcfg.SSE=1: U-mode and VU-mode ssrdp return ssp, and ssamoswap reaches memory (store/AMO
//     access fault with satp/vsatp Bare).
//   5. menvcfg.SSE=0: ssamoswap in VU-mode is illegal-instruction (the virtual case needs
//     menvcfg.SSE=1).
//
